Desktop Pet — Third-Party Notices
=================================

This project (MIT) bundles or depends on the following third-party components.
Their licenses and notices are reproduced/pointed to below.


1. Live2D renderer (`plugins/pet_live2d/`)
------------------------------------------
An in-repo Flutter plugin (first-party, MIT like the rest of this project) that
renders Live2D Cubism models. It replaces the third-party `live2d_flutter`
plugin, which was removed; the patches we carried for it are documented in
doc/live2d-renderer-notes.md.

It links against the Live2D Cubism Core / Cubism Native SDK — see below. The
SDK subset is not committed: it is fetched at setup time into third_party/live2d/
(gitignored) by tool/fetch_live2d_sdk.ps1, which keeps the SDK's own license
files alongside the extracted sources and binaries. The build **statically links
the Cubism Core** into pet_live2d_plugin.dll, so a distributed build embeds that
Core binary even though this repository does not contain it.


